Audit found a real accessibility gap: since `live.tsx` always passes `onLongPress`, the `Pressable` collapses the whole card into one node and only announced `props.name` — location, stars, trust tier, and friend/muted chips were invisible to screen-reader users. Fixed by building a combined `accessibilityLabel` from name + location + chips (excluding the ticking timer chip, to avoid relabeling the focused element every second). `tsc --noEmit` shows no new errors. RESULT written to `tasks/admin-queue/done/111-partner-chrome-pass2-RESULT.md` — COMPLETE, connect risk none.
